        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ONE_MOVE_PER_STATE",
        "derived": true,
        "holds": true,
        "statement": "ONE SERVO MOVE PER STATE: each state in an axis's auto list maps to exactly one Positions[i] in the staging rung. MAM edge-fires once per rung false→true, so a state can only ever command one move per axis. A multi-speed stroke is ONE MAM to the final target plus an MCD speed change at the transition point (Jason 2026-08-25) — the speed-change segment states are keyed on the MCD rung and are NOT in the MAM list.",
        "evidence": [
          "S00_IndexerNoSP.L5X R04_IndexerServo (IndexerAxis): auto states [13]",
          "S00_IndexerSP.L5X R04_IndexerServo (IndexerAxis): auto states [13]",
          "S00_IndexerSP.L5X R05_ShotPinServo (ShotPinAxis): auto states [7,19] each map to one position index (multi-position states: none)",
          "S05_ServoPNP.L5X R04_XAxisServo (XAxis): auto states [16,31,103,106] each map to one position index (multi-position states: none)",
          "S05_ServoPNP.L5X R05_ZAxisServo (ZAxis): auto states [7,13,22,28,100] each map to one position index (multi-position states: none)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "NO_CONSECUTIVE_SAME_AXIS_MOVES",
        "derived": true,
        "holds": true,
        "statement": "No two R02-adjacent states are both in one axis's MAM state list (the rung would never drop false, so the second move would never execute). Back-to-back DISTINCT moves on one axis use the trigger/wait split: move state → wait/confirm state not in the list → next move state. Fast/slow segments of ONE stroke are not two moves — they are one MAM plus an MCD speed change (Jason 2026-08-25).",
        "evidence": [
          "S00_IndexerNoSP.L5X R04_IndexerServo: adjacent-pair violations: none",
          "S00_IndexerSP.L5X R04_IndexerServo: adjacent-pair violations: none",
          "S00_IndexerSP.L5X R05_ShotPinServo: adjacent-pair violations: none",
          "S05_ServoPNP.L5X R04_XAxisServo: adjacent-pair violations: none",
          "S05_ServoPNP.L5X R05_ZAxisServo: adjacent-pair violations: none"
        ]
      },
